# PreBase desktop provider credentials
#
# The local PreBase/Magnus desktop extension does NOT read provider keys from
# this file. Add provider credentials in the PreBase provider UI; VS Code keeps
# them in OS-backed SecretStorage. Do not put user provider credentials in a
# workspace-local .env file, even when that file is ignored.
#
# Server-side development secrets belong in the deployment secret manager, not
# in this file. Never commit real credentials.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- PreBase cloud (Supabase) — development project ref mvfopbkhftgmcwdpqrww ---
# Publishable key only; never commit service role or secret keys.
# For the desktop IDE, set user settings (not committed):
#   "prebase.cloud.url": "https://mvfopbkhftgmcwdpqrww.supabase.co"
#   "prebase.cloud.publishableKey": "<from Supabase Dashboard → API → publishable key>"
# SUPABASE_URL=https://mvfopbkhftgmcwdpqrww.supabase.co
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Edge function / server secrets: Dashboard or `supabase secrets set` only.
